beral","person_id":"tvfy_10509","person_slug":"marise-payne","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Matthew Canavan","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10827","person_slug":"matthew-canavan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Michael Ronaldson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10550","person_slug":"michael-ronaldson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nick McKim","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10841","person_slug":"nick-mckim","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick Xenophon","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10717","person_slug":"nick-xenophon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nova Peris","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10820","person_slug":"nova-peris","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ricky Muir","party":"Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party","person_id":"tvfy_10834","person_slug":"ricky-muir","vote":"no"},{"name":"Robert Simms","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10842","person_slug":"robert-simms","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Bills — Social Services Legislation Amendment (Family Payments Structural Reform and Participation Measures) Bill 2015; First Reading","noes":11,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2015-11-30.142.2) that the [*Social Services Legislation Amendment (Family Payments Structural Reform and Participation Measures) Bill 2015*](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/r5557) be read a first time. Passing this motion means that the bills can be introduced into the Senate. [According to The Parliament](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/r5557#sched), this bill: > Amends the [A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999](http://www.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/cth/consol_act/antsaa1999357/) to restructure family tax benefit Part B by removing the benefit for couple families (other than grandparents or great-grandparents) with a youngest child 13 years of age or over. According to [Odgers’ Australian Senate Practice](http://www.aph.gov.au/About_Parliament/Senate/Powers_practice_n_procedures/odgers13?file=chapter12§ion=05), “the first reading is normally passed without opposition and is regarded as a purely formal stage”. That the Senate [divided to vote on this motion, rather than passing it “on the voices”](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/help/faq#division-occur), suggests that the [amendments](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Famend%2Fr5557_amend_1024de59-f06b-4722-9ffe-f189a44de518%22;rec=0) to the [*A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999*](http://www.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/cth/consol_act/antsaa1999357/) included in this bill were controversial.","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4006","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-11-30/1"}
